{ "data": { "text": "Next, using FreeSurfer's automated cortical parcellation [79], we obtained a classification of each subjects' cortical surface into 66 anatomical regions (33 per hemisphere), corresponding to the cortical regions defined in the Desikan-Killiany atlas [50]. For each subject and listening condition (i.e., quiet and noisy), node-averaged vectors ( V ) were extracted containing the functional data from the stimulus blocks corresponding to the listening condition of interest, and pair-wise, zero time-lag Pearson's correlations were calculated between nodes. This established a raw correlation matrix ( R ) containing the pair-wise correlations of the fMRI responses between each pair of cortical regions for each listening condition.\n\nSubsequently, we defined weighted cortical graphs G by assigning undirected, weighted connections (edges) between nodes whose absolute pair-wise correlation exceeded a pre-specified cost threshold, rc. This resulted in a weighted adjacency matrix ( W ), such that Wij = |Rij| if |Rij| ≥ rc or Wij = 0 if |Rij| < rc. The cost thresholds ( rc ) were specified separately for each subject in order to generate networks with fixed costs (i.e., the fraction of existing to possible edges in the network). To ensure that results were not dependent on any particular network cost, we constructed networks over a cost range from 0.10 to 0.40 at increments of 0.02.\n\nSmall-world networks possess Eglob approaching (but slightly less than) that of comparable random networks (i.e., Eglob ≲ Erandglob), and Eloc greater than random networks (i.e., Eloc ≳ Erandloc). Since differences in mean connection strengths affect the values of Eglob and Eloc, we computed normalized Eglob (Eglob/Erandglob) and Eloc (Eloc/Erandloc) by dividing the network properties by the average values obtained in 50 randomized surrogate networks of conserved size and connectivity distribution [83]. To reduce the number of statistical comparisons, we computed summary measures by averaging the normalized Eglob and Eloc values across the entire network cost curves (for both the nodal and network average measures)." }, "annotations": [ { "result": [ { "from_name": "Atlas definition", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 167, "end": 189, "text": "Desikan-Killiany atlas", "labels": [ "Atlas definition — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Atlas definition", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 167, "end": 189, "text": "1", "labels": [ "Atlas definition — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "ROI definition", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 106, "end": 126, "text": "66 anatomical regions", "labels": [ "ROI definition — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "ROI definition", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 127, "end": 147, "text": "33 per hemisphere", "labels": [ "ROI definition — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "ROI definition", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 12, "end": 53, "text": "FreeSurfer's automated cortical parcellation", "labels": [ "ROI definition — Software" ] } }, { "from_name": "ROI definition", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 106, "end": 126, "text": "2", "labels": [ "ROI definition — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Time series ROI", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 243, "end": 262, "text": "node-averaged vectors", "labels": [ "Time series ROI — Algorithm/Type" ] } }, { "from_name": "Time series ROI", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 243, "end": 262, "text": "3", "labels": [ "Time series ROI — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Compute connectivity", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 361, "end": 380, "text": "Pearson's correlations", "labels": [ "Compute connectivity — Algorithm" ] } }, { "from_name": "Compute connectivity", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 345, "end": 358, "text": "zero time-lag", "labels": [ "Compute connectivity — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Compute connectivity", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 361, "end": 380, "text": "4", "labels": [ "Compute connectivity — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Graph characteristics", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 477, "end": 498, "text": "undirected, weighted", "labels": [ "Graph characteristics — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Graph characteristics", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 604, "end": 627, "text": "weighted adjacency matrix", "labels": [ "Graph characteristics — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Graph characteristics", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 477, "end": 498, "text": "5", "labels": [ "Graph characteristics — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Negative correlation", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 536, "end": 562, "text": "absolute pair-wise correlation", "labels": [ "Negative correlation — Type" ] } }, { "from_name": "Negative correlation", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 536, "end": 543, "text": "6", "labels": [ "Negative correlation — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Sparsity control", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 730, "end": 740, "text": "fixed costs", "labels": [ "Sparsity control — Algorithm/Type" ] } }, { "from_name": "Sparsity control", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 902, "end": 928, "text": "cost range from 0.10 to 0.40", "labels": [ "Sparsity control — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Sparsity control", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 932, "end": 952, "text": "increments of 0.02", "labels": [ "Sparsity control — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Sparsity control", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 730, "end": 740, "text": "7", "labels": [ "Sparsity control — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Graph measures", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1016, "end": 1037, "text": "global ( Eglob )", "labels": [ "Graph measures — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Graph measures", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1042, "end": 1061, "text": "local ( Eloc )", "labels": [ "Graph measures — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Graph measures", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1016, "end": 1037, "text": "8", "labels": [ "Graph measures — Step Number" ] } }, { "from_name": "Result aggregation", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1318, "end": 1350, "text": "50 randomized surrogate networks", "labels": [ "Result aggregation — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Result aggregation", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1507, "end": 1536, "text": "averaging the normalized", "labels": [ "Result aggregation — Algorithm/Type" ] } }, { "from_name": "Result aggregation", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1560, "end": 1597, "text": "across the entire network cost curves", "labels": [ "Result aggregation — Parameters" ] } }, { "from_name": "Result aggregation", "to_name": "text", "type": "labels", "value": { "start": 1507, "end": 1536, "text": "9", "labels": [ "Result aggregation — Step Number" ] } } ] } ] }